logstalgia
------------------------------------------
Logstalgia is a visualization tool that replays or streams web server access
logs as a retro arcade game simulation.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.10-1
  libGLEW2.1-2.1.0-1
  libGLU1-9.0.3-1
  libSDL2_2.0_0-2.32.70-1
  libSDL2_image2.0_0-2.0.2-1
  libboost_filesystem1.66-1.66.0-1
  libboost_system1.66-1.66.0-1
  libfreetype6-2.13.3-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libpcre2_8_0-10.47-1
  libpng16-1.6.47-2
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-15-3
  autoconf-archive-2024.10.16-1
  automake-20250528-1
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.7-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libGLEW-devel-2.1.0-1
  libGLU-devel-9.0.3-1
  libSDL2-devel-2.32.70-1
  libSDL2_image-devel-2.0.2-1
  libboost-devel-1.66.0-1
  libfreetype-devel-2.13.3-1
  libpcre2-devel-10.47-1
  libpng-devel-1.6.47-2
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://logstalgia.io/

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/acaudwell/Logstalgia/releases/download/logstalgia-1.1.5/logstalgia-1.1.5.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack logstalgia-1.1.5-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./logstalgia-1.1.5-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/logstalgia-1.1.5-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/logstalgia-1.1.5-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(logstalgia)
  /usr/bin/logstalgia.exe
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/logstalgia.README
  /usr/share/doc/logstalgia/COPYING
  /usr/share/doc/logstalgia/ChangeLog
  /usr/share/doc/logstalgia/README
  /usr/share/doc/logstalgia/THANKS
  /usr/share/logstalgia/ball.tga
  /usr/share/logstalgia/example.log
  /usr/share/logstalgia/fonts/FreeMonoBold.ttf
  /usr/share/logstalgia/fonts/FreeSerif.ttf
  /usr/share/logstalgia/fonts/README
  /usr/share/logstalgia/glow.tga
  /usr/share/man/man1/logstalgia.1.gz

